# Low-friction UI

Choosing or adding something should happen in the control itself. Do not add a second button that only confirms what the user already chose.

**Do this:**

- A search list: arrow keys move the highlight, Enter or a click adds the highlighted row, then clear the field and leave the cursor there.
- A menu of known items (a campaign, a saved encounter): choosing an item performs the action and resets the menu to its placeholder.
- A short text field (a name): Enter submits, clears the field, and keeps focus.

**Do not do this:**

- An Add button beside a select or a one-line text field.
- A copies menu when one item per action is enough.

See creature search, campaign characters, saved encounters, and the name field in `obsidian/src/table-view.js`.
